90bd7f55b45eaa","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/squareup/README.md","size":20936,"sha256":"74b3cf984b89d947c30b600d9e36b4e5ecbf98535739c0f189b8b4841702894a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/attio/README.md","size":12684,"sha256":"bff8655a2e7ec5692e86d6fd5d0633b3db41e517bb7004de5db1918ff7ef340a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"references/cal-com/README.md","size":15178,"sha256":"7067963512d951fdd772f6f9b1276d1089f373363cc3736d86830309af38dfd4","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2329,"sha256":"c7948469af0a1e3dea3c12c256b46ef6c0ebe2cf41887bbe15f4aa5b00f79c6e","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1791054342619,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"76a9afcd5e42e3d1ac08bd793b288d2c27bb94355aace5f22d14d06a283c3174","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/76a9afcd5e42e3d1ac08bd793b288d2c27bb94355aace5f22d14d06a283c3174","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1790971310468},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":34,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":14,"checkedAt":1791054342619},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This is a broad but clearly disclosed API gateway skill for user-connected services, with sensitive actions mostly governed by explicit confirmation and least-privilege instructions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Network access, Bash, and a Maton account are proportionate for calling connected APIs. The raw gateway command is powerful, but its use is central to the skill and bounded by connected-app credentials and confirmation instructions.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Installation is via pinned Maton CLI packages and `maton login`; the inspected artifact contains Markdown and JSON reference files, with no bundled executable scripts or hidden install-time code.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"Root instructions default to read/list operations, require explicit confirmation for writes and high-impact actions, prohibit credential extraction, and treat external content as untrusted. Some provider reference examples lack endpoint-specific privacy or irreversibility warnings, but they do not contradict the central safety policy.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill discloses persistent OAuth/profile storage, persistent trigger destinations, hosted functions, and watch checkpoints. These are high-impact capabilities, but the instructions require user approval, least-privilege summaries, and cleanup for persistent automation.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill intentionally enables reads, writes, triggers, webhooks, serverless functions, and limited local event handlers for many connected third-party apps; that is broad and high-impact, but it matches the stated API-gateway purpose and is disclosed in the root instructions.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"note"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust Maton and intend to let an agent call APIs for services you have connected. Before approving actions, verify the exact connected account, target resource, recipients, data being sent or retrieved, and whether the action creates persistent forwarding, automation, hosted code, or irreversible deletion. Avoid broad OAuth scopes and delete unused connections, destinations, and functions when the task is finished.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: Acuity appointment and client examples can expose client personal data; this is expected for a scheduling API reference, though local read-side privacy guidance could be stronger.\n[SQP-2] expected: Calendly webhook deletion is a real persistent integration change; root DELETE/write confirmation applies, but the deletion example is less explicit than the adjacent webhook creation warning.\n[SQP-2] expected: GetResponse newsletter, transactional email, SMS, and import examples are expected marketing-platform capabilities; central write confirmation applies, but local recipient/data-upload warnings are incomplete.\n[SQP-2] expected: Mailchimp permanent delete, campaign scheduling, automation start, and queueing a subscriber are high-impact but purpose-aligned; several examples should carry stronger endpoint-local warnings despite the global confirmation policy.\n[SDI-4] expected: The PostHog project example includes a redacted `api_token` field; live responses may contain sensitive fields, so agents should redact them, but the artifact does not instruct credential disclosure.\n[SDI-1] expected: The Sunsama `delete_email_thread` schema is destructive, but its own description explicitly says it permanently removes messages and requires confirming the thread subject and account.\n[SQP-2] expected: Telegram send/media/contact/location examples are expected bot API writes; global write confirmation applies, while endpoint-local disclosure guidance for chat visibility is uneven.\n[SQP-2] expected: Twilio address creation sends personal or business address data to Twilio; this is purpose-aligned but should be handled with explicit confirmation and minimization.\n[SQP-2] expected: Unbounce lead reads expose personal lead data; this is expected CRM/landing-page behavior, though read examples should encourage minimization and redaction.\n[SQP-2] expected: Telegram command and profile mutations persistently alter bot behavior or presentation; global write confirmation applies, but local examples could state persistence more clearly.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1791054342619}}}}}